al_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.dev3.official [f4af8201b]\nv4.3.stable.mono.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev3 - Windows 10.0.19045 - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI recently opened a [discussion](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/11289) suggesting to add the \"extend script\" button to the top of the scene tree dock and user @Flynsarmy discovered that surprisingly, the button already _does_ exist there, but for some reason never shows up. This seems like a bug, as the intended behavior seems to be to show the extend script button when selecting a custom type but that doesn't happen. (See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1f47e4c4e3a09a422e96880a7918d986dd575a63/editor/scene_tree_dock.cpp#L2802-L2810)\nI'm not an expert on Godot architecture by any means, so maybe this isn't what I think it is, but I figured it was worth reporting because it's a quality of life feature I'd like to see added to the engine and it doesn't seem well known.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1aeb3e2-49ec-4fe9-9499-95c8692de333)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Follow the steps to create a new plugin\n- Create a script to represent a custom type and initialize it in the plugin script\n- Restart the editor\n- Add your custom type to the scene tree and select it\n- Although the scene tree dock code suggests that the extend script button should show up, it doesn't\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18030489/mrp.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"afterlightgames","id":86094024,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDk0MDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86094024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterlightgames","html_url":"https://github.com/afterli